  "goodToKnow": "Das Examen is a major final exam, especially at university: das Staatsexamen, required for law, medicine, pharmacy and in many states teaching, is set by the state rather than the university. Law students face two Staatsexamen, notoriously tough. For everyday exams, Germans say die Prüfung or die Klausur. The plural is die Examen or, formally, die Examina."
